{
  "item": "28.10b nomic query/document prompts, re-measured after the relevance-gated chunk window and fixed candidate pool (76d0824)",
  "date": "2026-10-03/04",
  "conclusion": "Keep nomic unprompted. On the dogfood eval the prompts trade 5 questions up for 5 down and drop 2 answers from the prompt hook's block; on LongMemEval they lower NDCG@10 0.947->0.914 (1 better, 5 worse) and recall_all 0.917->0.875. The rescoring window was not the reason they lost.",
  "method": {
    "builds": "off = dev c4e2d80 (every model unprompted); on = dev c4e2d80 + revert of 90880bd (nomic search_query:/search_document:, text_prefixes store marker, reembed --table guard)",
    "search": "exact vector scan (one-shot CLI scans exactly below 100k vectors), so runs repeat",
    "dogfood": "benchmarks/dogfood-recall/run.py, 57 questions; snapshots snap-nomic-off (embedded without prompts, no marker) and snap-nomic-on (embedded with search_document:, marker set); --fetch 10 and 25",
    "longmemeval": "LongMemEval-S, strategy recall-qtc, top-k 5, --model nomic, --jobs 1; 24 questions = the first 4 of each question type in the deterministic s60 sample (every k-th question of each type in dataset order); each question run off then on as a pair",
    "control": "the unchanged dev binary and the revert build give identical per-question results on snap-nomic-off (k10): the revert changes nothing for stores without the marker"
  },
